  "body": "## What fails\n\nPost-merge run 44493729434 on `main` at `70b5c5916` has the result `failure`.\nThe batch gate reports: `wall 58.3 min, 913 step(s), 3 failed`.\n\nOne failed step is new: `app suites: shoulder_adaptive` (8 s). These tests fail:\n\n- `fig8_bottom_face_outside_containment_generates_and_stops_at_face`\n- `fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`\n- `outside_containment_air_band_fixture_blocks_post`\n\nThe other two failed steps are `kernel suites: step_agreement` and `app suites: feature_edge_g1_join`. Issue #2713 tracks them.\n\n## When it started\n\nRun 44484318680 at `3e615d653` had 2 failed steps of 912. `shoulder_adaptive` was green there.\nThus one of these merges causes the failure:\n\n- #2730 at `298bea307`\n- #2665 at `a4e5a68ab`\n- #2731 at `b02b344d6`\n- #1798 at `70b5c5916`\n\nThe runs for the three commits between the two were cancelled by later pushes.\n\n## What is not known\n\nThe `--log-failed` output of the run has the test names only. It does not have the assert text.\nThe `report` job was skipped, thus no issue was updated automatically (#1611).\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Run `cargo xtask gate test` for the binary `shoulder_adaptive` of `camcraft-app` on `origin/main`.\n2. Record the assert text of each test in a comment here.\n3. Find the merge that causes the failure.\n4. Correct the cause. Do not weaken a test that guards the post block.\n\nIf `outside_containment_air_band_fixture_blocks_post` fails because a post passes that must be blocked, raise this issue to `P1`.\n",
